Counselor drift brief generated at 2026-08-31T10:32:00Z.
This brief reads durable records only, offers advice, and makes no decision or refusal.
Window rule: Each observation is a completed half-open Coordinated Universal Time calendar week that carries retained evidence, plus the most recently completed week; the active week is excluded.

Spend versus outcome compares completed governed and tracked run time with current-branch Git landings in the same window.
Cost: During 2026-08-03 through 2026-08-10 (end excluded), the governed run count was 0 with 0 minutes spent, and the retained tracked run count was 0 with 0 minutes spent.
Run outcomes during that window were governed green 0, red 0, ended unknown 0, and launch failed 0; retained tracked green 0, red 0, ended unknown 0, and launch failed 0.
Git landing count was 267, touching 988 files with 61578 text insertions; 0 binary files had no insertion count.
Cost: During 2026-08-10 through 2026-08-17 (end excluded), the governed run count was 0 with 0 minutes spent, and the retained tracked run count was 0 with 0 minutes spent.
Git landing count was 656, touching 2657 files with 147678 text insertions; 0 binary files had no insertion count.
Cost: During 2026-08-17 through 2026-08-24 (end excluded), the governed run count was 0 with 0 minutes spent, and the retained tracked run count was 0 with 0 minutes spent.
Git landing count was 467, touching 1801 files with 69388 text insertions; 0 binary files had no insertion count.
Cost: During 2026-08-24 through 2026-08-31 (end excluded), the governed run count was 0 with 0 minutes spent, and the retained tracked run count was 0 with 0 minutes spent.
Git landing count was 813, touching 3052 files with 137194 text insertions; 0 binary files had no insertion count.
Limitation — Risk-class evidence: Current durable records carry landing counts and size but no landing risk class, so this signal reports spend versus outcome and makes no risk verdict. Enrichment: Record a risk class with each landing.
Limitation — Threshold history: Configuration exposes a current scalar validation-weight threshold, but durable run and landing records do not preserve which threshold was effective in each window, so the brief makes no threshold comparison. Enrichment: Record the effective threshold value and its source with each weight generation.
Limitation — Causal attribution: Run spend and Git landings are aggregated by completion time in the same week; records do not identify which proof caused or validated which commit. Enrichment: Carry the landing commit identifier on governed attempts and retained tracked-run outcomes.
Limitation — Tracked-run retention: Ordinary tracked runs are represented only while their run records are retained; acknowledged terminal records can be pruned and ungoverned identifiers can be reused. Enrichment: Add a non-prunable terminal ledger for ordinary tracked runs.
Limitation — Window resolution: Delivery follows the repository's counselor cadence, while the signal windows remain completed Coordinated Universal Time calendar weeks and omit the active partial week and empty older weeks. Enrichment: Record finer-grained durable evidence before producing windows shorter than one week.
Limitation — Landing size: Git numstat supplies insertion counts for text paths; binary paths have no insertion count and merge commits may carry no numstat payload. Enrichment: Record byte sizes and an explicit merge-payload attribution rule.

Process versus product compares retained goal-ledger operations and non-carrier record-only landings with concluded goals and product landings.
Classification rule: Goal events are deduplicated by operation identifier. Exact open, edit, claim, and set-budget events plus non-carrier record-only landings are process activities; exact done events plus product landings are product outcomes. A Git landing whose Goal-Transaction trailer matches a counted goal operation is that operation's carrier, is shown separately, and is not counted again. Every other landing is record-only when it changes at least one path and every changed path is under memory/, plans/, or records/. A landing with any other changed path is product, and a landing with no numstat path is unclassified.
During 2026-08-03 through 2026-08-10 (end excluded), the retained goal history recorded 0 open, 0 edit, 0 claim, 0 explicit budget, and 0 done operations; Git landing classes were non-carrier record-only 136, matched goal-operation carrier 0, product 120, and unclassified 11.
Cost: The process-versus-product activity ratio is 1.13, from 136 process activities divided by 120 product outcomes.
During 2026-08-10 through 2026-08-17 (end excluded), the retained goal history recorded 0 open, 0 edit, 0 claim, 0 explicit budget, and 0 done operations; Git landing classes were non-carrier record-only 203, matched goal-operation carrier 0, product 453, and unclassified 0.
Cost: The process-versus-product activity ratio is 0.45, from 203 process activities divided by 453 product outcomes.
During 2026-08-17 through 2026-08-24 (end excluded), the retained goal history recorded 29 open, 63 edit, 60 claim, 0 explicit budget, and 44 done operations; Git landing classes were non-carrier record-only 62, matched goal-operation carrier 196, product 205, and unclassified 4.
Cost: The process-versus-product activity ratio is 0.86, from 214 process activities divided by 249 product outcomes.
During 2026-08-24 through 2026-08-31 (end excluded), the retained goal history recorded 86 open, 156 edit, 65 claim, 37 explicit budget, and 48 done operations; Git landing classes were non-carrier record-only 79, matched goal-operation carrier 392, product 339, and unclassified 3.
Cost: The process-versus-product activity ratio is 1.09, from 423 process activities divided by 387 product outcomes.
Limitation — Goal-event exclusions: 62 unique retained goal operations use verbs outside the requested exact mapping and were excluded from the ratio. Enrichment: Record a closed activity class on every goal operation.
Limitation — Path classification: The product count is a path proxy: every landing with a path outside memory/, plans/, and records/ is product, so non-code files outside those roots are included. Enrichment: Publish a repository-owned code-path projection and carry it with landing records.
Limitation — Goal-verb coverage: Only exact open, edit, claim, set-budget, and done history verbs are classified. Combined open-claim and every other verb are excluded because history has no closed activity-class field; a claim line also does not reveal an implicit budget. Enrichment: Add a closed activity class to each goal-history event, including combined operations.
Limitation — Goal-history retention: The signal reads retained live, concluded, and legacy goal files; pruning can remove concluded records, so this is not guaranteed all-time activity. Enrichment: Retain an append-only goal-event journal independent of pruned goal files.
Limitation — Register-edit classification: Registers and receipts both resolve under the broad memory/ record root, so register edits cannot be separated from other record-only landings and remain inside that count. Enrichment: Publish a dedicated register path or a durable typed landing class that distinguishes register edits from other records.
Limitation — Cross-source attribution: A matching Goal-Transaction trailer prevents a counted goal operation's carrier commit from being counted twice. A goal-record change without a matching trailer cannot be joined, so a mixed product commit can still contribute both a goal event and a product landing. Enrichment: Require every goal-record mutation to retain its goal operation identifier in the landing commit.
Limitation — Goal-carrier reconciliation: 60 Git landings carried Goal-Transaction identifiers that did not match a classified retained goal operation; those landings were classified by path instead of being silently discarded. Enrichment: Restore the matching retained goal history or add a closed activity class for the operation's verb.
